<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  NuVoxel Keypad — Control4 DriverWorks driver (per-device)
  One instance per keypad, placed in the keypad's room. Connects OUT to the
  device (which is the TCP server) and reads the room's now-playing state,
  relays transport/volume/source, and hosts the SIP intercom endpoint.
  Protocol: see ../PROTOCOL.md

  WHY A NEW FILENAME (NuVoxelKeypad.c4z, not MediaKeypad.c4z):
  Control4 instantiates a driver's proxies ONLY when the driver is first ADDED to
  a project. Changing the <proxy> set of an already-installed driver corrupts the
  project (it has crashed a Director in this repo). This driver restructures the
  proxy set — it absorbs the former companion "Media Keypad Intercom" driver as a
  third proxy (5003) — so it MUST ship under a filename that has never been
  installed anywhere. Never reuse MediaKeypad.c4z for this.
-->
